{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"id":"NIT-265","uuid":"8224e439-786b-483c-9970-039dec60898d","title":"Build faithful Neatlogs replica and APIs","description":"## Agreed scope; ready for independent implementation\n\n**Decision recorded 11 October 2026:** build a basic buyer-led Tailor proof of concept. Tailor is intended for software companies; Neatlogs is the first example. This ticket is the complete first build slice, including reference inspection, data contracts, developer harness and verification. The bounded replica scope is settled and ready for implementation when Nitin launches the coding session. <issue id=\"193a97a8-bd29-45e5-bfba-dd1d7c790ca8\" href=\"https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-253/review-proof-plan-and-decide-next-step\">NIT-253</issue> can run in parallel and does not need to be completed before this ticket starts. This Linear correction launches no coding session and is not a commitment to the full commercial product.\n\n## Outcome and scope\n\nA visitor starts on a faithful limited replica of the current Neatlogs public landing page, opens a Tailor entry CTA (proposed label: “Try with your project”), describes an existing/planned project, then freely explores the supported synthetic demo. Save that description and the demo state during and after the visit so the vendor can inspect the session. For this slice, use two clearly labelled deterministic fixtures. **Saving text does not generate personalization; no LLM or agent exists in this slice.** Make that limitation explicit in the UI.\n\nIncluded:\n\n* Public landing/entry flow; app shell matching the current real Neatlogs product.\n* Trace list and trace detail, including span tree, timeline, inputs/outputs, errors and timing.\n* Relevant search/filters for this trace workflow, with truthful counts and empty states.\n* List → detail → Back/Forward, direct trace/span links and reload.\n* Basic typed APIs, one persistent canonical dataset per session, and a developer-only fixture/validation harness.\n* Minimal developer/vendor inspection of saved input and scenario state. A full vendor dashboard and full authentication are outside scope; use fictional/local sessions until access and retention are agreed.\n\n**Visual fidelity to actual current Neatlogs is a dealbreaker.** Do not invent a generic observability dashboard or use the older approximate Paper designs as design truth.\n\n## Inputs and reference inspection\n\nRepository: [https://github.com/nitink133/tailor-neathack](<https://github.com/nitink133/tailor-neathack>)\nParallel agent discussion and post-replica review: [NIT-253](<https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-253>)\nSetup evidence: [NIT-252](<https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-252>)\nSandbox catalogue: [https://chatgpt.com/space/page_3bf8c65eb9248191b298a09646a631d6](<https://chatgpt.com/space/page_3bf8c65eb9248191b298a09646a631d6>)\nBackground workshop: [https://chatgpt.com/space/page_a57ae2efb9808191ab50b99c369d35cf](<https://chatgpt.com/space/page_a57ae2efb9808191ab50b99c369d35cf>)\nPublic design: [https://neatlogs.com/](<https://neatlogs.com/>)\nRead-only authenticated sandbox: [https://app.neatlogs.com/traces?orgId=8186e5df-b745-4e66-a01d-94c420459c43&projectId=a35a7334-258e-441c-b2e1-b8198a263f21&f=tags\\~tailor-demo-20261010-v1](<https://app.neatlogs.com/traces?orgId=8186e5df-b745-4e66-a01d-94c420459c43&projectId=a35a7334-258e-441c-b2e1-b8198a263f21&f=tags~tailor-demo-20261010-v1>)\n\nThe workshop and [historical runtime research](<https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-268>) predate the selected replica direction. Follow this ticket when they conflict.\n\nBefore UI implementation, inspect the public landing and logged-in Tailor Demo Sandbox using **Nitin's personal Mac / Comet**, read-only. Capture safe screenshots and behavior notes for the included surfaces, including layout, typography, spacing, controls, status semantics, selected-span behavior, navigation, loading/error/empty states and representative filter results. Label reference dates/viewports. Discover the exact fields and controls within the agreed surfaces through this read-only inspection; that detail discovery is implementation work, not a new product-scope approval gate. No real-account changes, injection or re-ingestion. If the reference browser is inaccessible, report the exact blocker and continue independent contract work; do not substitute guessed UI. Confirm trace outcome versus child-error badges from observed behavior.\n\nThe existing sandbox's 10 traces / 47 spans / 9 sessions and 40 saved manual rubric answers are reference/teaching evidence only. Four optional expansion cases remain unresolved (two Processing failed, two not found, cause unknown). That expansion and the parked Analytics discrepancy do not block a controlled replica.\n\n## Repository and Entire preflight\n\n* Inspect the current repository, its README/package scripts, root AGENTS.md and relevant .agents/skills. Fetch origin/main, record its actual SHA, and use a **new feature branch and separate worktree from that freshly fetched main**.\n* Last verified main supplied by the setup session: **9ba9a45f6d8fa916a56bcee31738ba57cc7e2b99**. It includes consolidated work, a relative AGENTS.md and project-local .agents/skills/entire-continuity. Verify rather than assume it is still latest.\n* The primary local checkout was dirty/stale. Do not reset, clean, overwrite, switch or reuse it. Preserve human/other-agent work and all existing refs.\n* Before each actual implementing session, follow the project-local Entire continuity skill and verify the live capture state for that exact session/branch. Healthy instructions/hooks alone are insufficient. Historical live CLI capture is proven; desktop UI capture remains untested. If capture cannot be verified, stop implementation and report.\n* Historical genuine checkpoint: **01M4M9KRQN7RM3S5SK606GSN8Q**; corresponding local/remote checkpoint-ref SHA **d15aeacf52215aff94ec4a887ba951652d254646**. These prove earlier capture, not this next session. Never fabricate a checkpoint or transcript.\n* Preserve the existing **real Tailor → Neatlogs observability integration**. The synthetic Neatlogs replica UI is demo content; it is a separate concern from real telemetry about Tailor execution.\n\n## API and data contract\n\nKeep implementation small and reuse appropriate existing code after inspection. Do not prescribe a new framework without evidence. Define typed request/response and error contracts before the UI consumes them.\n\nOne canonical session dataset must support:\n\n* Creation/readback of a demo session with saved visitor input and immutable session ownership/boundary.\n* Read/query projections for trace list and filters, trace detail, span tree/timeline and I/O/errors/timing.\n* Versioned scenario state and a developer-only operation for selecting/proposing a supported fixture.\n* Deterministic validation, atomic publication and actual readback of the accepted version; stale, invalid or partial updates leave the previous good version intact.\n* Stable trace/span/session IDs; valid parent relationships; consistent timings and status semantics; no cross-session data exposure.\n* Persistence across navigation, reload and server restart, sufficient for later vendor review. Document where data lives and how the local test dataset can be reset; no real buyer-data collection, public exposure or indefinite-retention promise.\n* Clear unknown-ID, unsupported-action, empty, loading and failure responses. Browser and API must agree on active scenario/version.\n\nThe developer harness uses the same APIs/contracts as the UI. It may choose deterministic fixtures, validate intentionally broken changes and inspect saved sessions. It must not pretend to interpret arbitrary project descriptions.\n\n## Two fixtures\n\n1. **Order lookup: first attempt fails, retry recovers.** The span tree shows failure and recovery; the final answer is correct for the fictional order.\n2. **Order lookup: both attempts fail.** Both failures, timings and final output agree; the agent safely escalates without inventing order data or claiming it contacted a real person.\n\nBoth are clearly synthetic. They use coherent linked records across every included view. Distinguish final task outcome from trace/child error indicators using observed Neatlogs semantics.\n\n## Acceptance and run evidence\n\n- [ ] Dated current-product reference screenshots and behavior/contract notes cover every included surface.\n- [ ] Side-by-side screenshots at matching viewports show faithful layout, type, controls and data hierarchy; every material deviation is listed for Nitin.\n- [ ] Both fixtures pass the same API/UI consistency checks. List counts, filters, trace IDs, span parents, timeline, input/output and final outcome agree.\n- [ ] A deliberately invalid/stale proposal is rejected without partial changes; a corrected update is atomically accepted and verified by independent readback.\n- [ ] Two fictional sessions remain isolated through API reads/updates and direct links. Neither can read or overwrite the other.\n- [ ] Back/Forward, direct links, reload, restart, repeated clicks and interrupted requests keep coherent state; unknown/unsupported actions fail honestly.\n- [ ] Visitor input and accepted state remain available for authorized local vendor/developer inspection after exploration.\n- [ ] Existing real observability/tests still work. No real account mutations, frontend credentials, model calls/spend or deployment.\n- [ ] Inspect and document the actual install/dev/API/fixture/reset/test/typecheck/lint/build commands in README or the repo's established runbook. Run all applicable repository checks on the final code; list passed, failed and not-run checks separately. Do not invent script names.\n- [ ] Return branch/base/final commit, changed files, run instructions, screenshots, fixture/validation evidence, real telemetry references where available, genuine session/checkpoint evidence and remaining limitations.\n\n## Non-goals and stop point\n\nNo browser JavaScript injection or response interception in the real Neatlogs account. No Analytics, Evals, built-in assistant, billing, full auth, calendar/audio, automatic product onboarding, multi-vendor platform or commercial naming work. Do not run model inference, claim arbitrary personalization, deploy, change sharing, push/merge or contact anyone merely because this ticket exists.\n\nStop for Nitin's review in [NIT-253](<https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-253>) after the deterministic replica/API proof. The later bounded agent loop is [NIT-269](<https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-269>), conditional on evidence and separate approval. Nitin decides continue, refine or stop.","priority":{"value":2,"name":"High"},"url":"https://linear.app/nitinkhanna/issue/NIT-265/build-faithful-neatlogs-replica-and-apis","gitBranchName":"work/nit-265-build-faithful-neatlogs-replica-and-apis","createdAt":"2026-10-10T05:47:38.710Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-11T02:06:16.374Z","archivedAt":null,"completedAt":null,"startedAt":null,"canceledAt":null,"dueDate":null,"slaStartedAt":null,"slaMediumRiskAt":null,"slaHighRiskAt":null,"slaBreachesAt":null,"status":"Todo","statusType":"unstarted","labels":[],"attachments":[],"documents":[],"stateHistory":[{"state":{"id":"41bd2ae0-083f-4708-8365-0be3e0b2396a","name":"In Progress","type":"started"},"startedAt":"2026-10-10T05:47:38.710Z","endedAt":"2026-10-11T01:53:24.046Z"},{"state":{"id":"d2ddd022-2c71-475d-a164-b1cf2cd973a5","name":"Todo","type":"unstarted"},"startedAt":"2026-10-11T01:53:24.046Z","endedAt":null}],"createdBy":"Nitin Khanna","createdById":"13310042-1c24-42e6-928e-e230315cfe26","project":"neatHack · October 2026","projectId":"b4864b4e-a7a7-4474-9097-43b0b63226f5","team":"Nitin","teamId":"5361032a-b2d5-40d3-bcc3-456b6ef6bdcb"}"}],"isError":false}
